ParseSmalltalk(source) -> shared evaluator nodes or error
    Lex identifiers, keywords, operators, literals, punctuation and source positions.
    Include backslash among binary operator characters, including literal selectors.
    Skip whitespace and double-quoted comments.
    Parse classes, fields, superclass names and unary/binary/keyword method bodies.
    Parse assignment, return, closures, arrays and messages with unary, binary, keyword and cascade precedence.
    Fold constructors, transcript output and JSON operations into evaluator forms.
    Optionally record exact selector token ranges for method headers and explicit sends.
ParseSmalltalkClassSource(source) -> class definition or error
    Parse source and extract its class definition through the shared class parser.
parseWorkspaceSource(source) -> shared evaluator nodes or error
    Use the Smalltalk front end for interactive workspace expressions.
